    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Kyle Tucker** (77.80) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.10). **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a soft matchup against McCullers Jr., where strong SP skill metrics elevate his floor, while **Jackson Merrill** draws a favorable start against Houser; despite Houser\u2019s decent pop time, **Jackson Merrill**\u2019s leadoff spot and aggressive plate approach maximize his scoring potential. **Gunnar Henderson** (74.77) also warrants attention; although his lineup status is pending, his matchup against a slow-working P\u00e9rez provides a distinct advantage in our SB-heavy scoring environment, effectively nullifying the slight negative park impact.\n\nThe most difficult decision for today's lineup was omitting **Nolan Schanuel** (59.14). While his projected efficiency remains solid, he narrowly missed the cut due to a logjam at the UTIL and corner infield spots where **Miguel Vargas** and **Brady House** offered higher upside against favorable arms like Ure\u00f1a and Ober. We are keeping a close eye on **Josh Jung**, who remains on the bench with a 51.20 score; while his matchup is decent, a 44% rain risk and the current stability of our primary infield starters make him an easy hold to protect against potential early game termination or truncated at-bats.\n\nWe are banking on these platoon edges to stabilize our AVG and RBI categories. **Sam Antonacci** (63.13) and **Miguel Vargas** (61.42) are both positioned to exploit Ure\u00f1a\u2019s high xERA, with **Sam Antonacci**\u2019s elite xwOBA metrics making him a high-leverage start. Conversely, we are exercising caution with **Jacob Wilson** (50.16) and **Heliot Ramos** (45.74); both face elite-caliber arms in Wheeler and Rodriguez, respectively, and will be on a short leash to ensure our game caps are reserved for more advantageous matchups moving forward.",
